WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.240
Every year, crowds of Shi'a pilgrims
travel to great domed shrines.

2
00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:09.030
Each one honours a man
Shi'a Muslims call an Imam:

3
00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:11.260
one in a line of twelve.

4
00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:13.690
Now walk into almost any mosque.

5
00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.350
Someone steps to the
front to lead the prayer.

6
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.410
He is called an imam too.

7
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:21.430
So is that the same word for the same job?

8
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:25.570
In this mission, you'll find out
who the Imams are for Shi'a Muslims,

9
00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.600
and why one word can carry two meanings.

10
00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:32.590
Then you'll set the two side by side,
and test what you've learned in a mosque

11
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:33.620
hall.

12
00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:38.840
Your mission: find out whether an imam
and an Imam really do the same job.
